<string name="onboarding_chapter_applying_apply_description">Apply your appliance as you would normally, to clean, dry skin. Press down to ensure tight fit. Also press down along the sensor layer arm.</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_applying_apply_title">Apply to body</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_applying_attach_description">Well done! Your transmitter is now successfully attached to the sensor layer under your baseplate. It\'s ready to look for signs of leakage and notify you on your phone.</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_applying_attach_title">Transmitter attached</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_applying_checklist_description">Let\'s take a look at how to apply TestProduct to the body.</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_applying_checklist_title">You\'re almost there!</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_applying_connector_flap_description">Identify the connector flap on the sensor layer. Lift the flap away from your body to prepare it for attaching your transmitter.</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_applying_connector_flap_title">Lift connector flap</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_applying_ensure_closed_description">Ensure the lid of the transmitter is fully closed before continuing. The lid should be level with front surface of the transmitter.</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_applying_ensure_closed_title">Ensure transmitter lid is closed</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_applying_identify_dark_description">Identify the dark grey side of your transmitter. This side should be facing your body when you come to attach it.</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_applying_identify_dark_title">Identify dark grey side</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_applying_lift_lid_description">From a closed position, lift the transmitter lid one \'click\', to set it in a fixed, lifted position.</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_applying_lift_lid_title">Lift transmitter lid</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_applying_locating_opening_description">Next, locate the opening of the transmitter.</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_applying_locating_opening_title">Locate transmitter opening</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_applying_prevent_damage_description">It\'s nearly time to attach your transmitter. It\'s important to attach your transmitter correctly to avoid any damage to your connection. To get you off to the best start, the following screens will guide you step-by-step on preparing your transmitter for proper attachment.</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_applying_prevent_damage_title">Attach your transmitter correctly to prevent damage</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_applying_ready_attach_description">Make sure to follow the step-by-step guidance closely to attach the transmitter correctly.</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_applying_ready_attach_title">Great. You\'re now ready to attach your transmitter.</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_applying_remove_sl_description">Carefully remove the sensor layer release liner, ensuring the sensor layer doesn\'t lift off the baseplate.</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_applying_remove_sl_title">Remove sensor layer release liner</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_applying_take_out_description">First, take your transmitter out of the charger.</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_applying_take_out_title">Take out transmitter</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_applying_transmitter_checker_button">I\'m not sure</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_applying_transmitter_checker_description">To check you\'re on the right track - which position is your transmitter lid in?</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_applying_transmitter_checker_option_1_description">Lid can only wiggle slightly.</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_applying_transmitter_checker_option_1_title">Lifted &amp; fixed</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_applying_transmitter_checker_option_2_description">Lid able to swing open easily.</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_applying_transmitter_checker_option_2_title">Lifted &amp; loose</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_applying_transmitter_checker_option_select">Select</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_applying_transmitter_checker_title">Just checking...</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_intro_bluetooth_description">TestProduct connects to your phone and communicates with it via Bluetooth. Keep Bluetooth on at all times to stay informed.\n\nYou’ll be asked to turn your Bluetooth on if it’s not on already. Your phone will also ask you to allow Bluetooth use.</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_intro_bluetooth_header">TestProduct needs Bluetooth to keep you informed</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_intro_bluetooth_settings_alert_message">Go to Settings to turn on Bluetooth. Then, come back to the app to continue setup.</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_intro_bluetooth_settings_alert_title">Turn on Bluetooth to Allow \"TestProduct\" to Connect to Accessories.</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_intro_box_description">Your TestProduct starter kit contains three components. Next, you\'ll take a look at them one by one.</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_intro_box_title">What\'s in the box?</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_intro_bullet_item_1">A flat surface, like a table or worktop</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_intro_bullet_item_2">Access to a power socket</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_intro_bullet_item_3">A USB plug (e.g. iPhone charger plug)</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_intro_bullet_item_4">Everything you currently use in your change routine</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_intro_bullet_list_description">As well as the TestProduct starter kit, you will also need:</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_intro_bullet_list_title">Before you get started…</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_intro_checklist_description">The guide includes videos to help you get started with your new product.</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_intro_checklist_item_1">1. Introduction</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_intro_checklist_item_2">2. Connecting</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_intro_checklist_item_3">3. Preparing</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_intro_checklist_item_4">4. Applying</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_intro_checklist_title">Welcome to the Setup guide</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_intro_connector_flap_description">This is the connector flap. You\'ll use this later to attach your transmitter to the sensor layer.</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_intro_connector_flap_title">Connector flap</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_intro_inner_outer_description">The sensors are arranged in two rings. The inner sensors detect the first signs of leakage. The outer sensors detect leakage spreading.</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_intro_inner_outer_title">Inner and outer sensors</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_intro_notifications_description">By allowing notifications, you enable TestProduct to notify you when leakage is detected. You can customise notification alerts later in the app\'s settings.</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_intro_notifications_header">Know when to take action by allowing notifications</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_intro_sensor_layer_description">This is a TestProduct sensor layer. It is applied to your ostomy appliance to help you detect leakage. You\'ll learn how to apply this later.</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_intro_sensor_layer_title">Sensor layer</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_intro_sensor_technology_description">On the reverse side, you can see the advanced sensor technology. Each layer has 68 leakage sensors, one under each of the small dots.</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_intro_sensor_technology_title">Advanced sensor technology</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_intro_setup_guide">Setup guide</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_intro_setup_guide_message">This guide will guide you step-by-step through the process of setting up TestProduct and applying in to your body.</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_preparing_change_come_back_later_button">I\'ll return later</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_preparing_change_description">During the next few steps, you will need to change your ostomy appliance. If now isn\'t a good time, you can return and complete the guide later.</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_preparing_change_title">It will soon be time to apply your new TestProduct</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_preparing_checklist_description">Next, you\'ll move on to preparing your appliance and sensor layer.</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_preparing_checklist_title">So far, so good</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_preparing_come_back_later_button">I\'m ready now</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_preparing_come_back_later_description">Simply come back to the app when you are ready to change your ostomy appliance. Your progress will be saved and you can pick up where you left off.</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_preparing_come_back_later_title">Take your time. Your setup guide will be waiting for you.</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_preparing_place_sl_description">With the turquoise ring facing up, place the sensor layer on your baseplate. The long sensor layer arm can point in the direction that suits you.</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_preparing_place_sl_title">Place sensor layer on baseplate</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_preparing_press_down_description">Press the sensor layer down firmly. Avoid touching the exposed baseplate adhesive as this could reduce adhesion to the body later.</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_preparing_press_down_title">Press down sensor layer</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_preparing_removing_description">Prepare your appliance as normal. Place it on a flat surface with the release liner facing up. Peel off the release liner on your baseplate.</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_preparing_removing_title">Remove release liner</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_preparing_secure_description">Circle around the sensor layer firmly several times, especially around the turquoise ring, to ensure secure adhesion to your baseplate.</string>
<string name="onboarding_chapter_preparing_secure_title">Ensure secure adhesion</string>
<string name="onboarding_confirmation_button">Continue</string>
<string name="onboarding_confirmation_description">Just a couple more steps to complete your profile before you can setting up TestProduct</string>
<string name="onboarding_confirmation_title">Profile saved</string>
